WEBVTT

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:32.213
Chapter 1 A spoiled little girl.

00:00:32.273 --> 00:00:52.334
Mary Lennox was spoiled, rude and had a bad temper.

00:00:52.394 --> 00:00:58.066
Because she was often ill, she was thin with a sad face.

00:00:58.126 --> 00:01:00.386
She complained a lot.

00:01:00.446 --> 00:01:03.027
No one liked her at all.

00:01:03.087 --> 00:01:06.278
This was not really Mary's fault.

00:01:06.338 --> 00:01:13.191
She lived in India with her mother and father, but she did not see her parents very often.

00:01:13.251 --> 00:01:24.909
Mary's father was busy with his work and her mother was a very beautiful woman who loved parties and was not interested in her small daughter.

00:01:24.969 --> 00:01:31.194
She left Mary in the care of an Indian nanny called an Aya.

00:01:31.253 --> 00:01:39.289
Her Aya let Mary do what she wanted because she didn't want Mary to cry and irritate her mother.

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:45.334
Mary soon became a spoiled and unpleasant young girl.

00:01:45.394 --> 00:01:54.210
When Mary was nine years old, she woke up one hot morning and felt that there was something wrong.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:02:03.046
She heard strange cries and shouts and the sound of feet outside her door, but no one came to see her.

00:02:03.105 --> 00:02:07.640
She went back to sleep.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:15.276
Later, when Mary woke up, the house was silent.

00:02:15.336 --> 00:02:17.988
She heard nothing.

00:02:18.047 --> 00:02:23.930
Mary was angry because no one came to bring her food or to dress her.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:31.334
Suddenly, her door opened and two Englishmen entered.

00:02:31.394 --> 00:02:34.496
Mary looked at them angrily.

00:02:34.556 --> 00:02:37.108
Why has everyone forgotten me?

00:02:37.168 --> 00:02:38.298
She asked.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.779
Where is my ire?

00:02:39.839 --> 00:02:41.710
Why does no one come?

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:43.351
For little kid.

00:02:43.411 --> 00:02:44.862
Said one of the men.

00:02:44.922 --> 00:02:46.754
There is nobody here.

00:02:46.814 --> 00:02:55.980
That is how Mary discovered that her mother and father were dead and that the servants were dead too because of a terrible disease.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.943
That was why the house was so silent.

00:03:00.002 --> 00:03:04.587
Mary Lennox was completely alone.

00:03:04.647 --> 00:03:19.236
There was no one in India to look after Mary, so she went to England to live with her uncle, Mr. Craven, who lived in a big house in Yorkshire called Misulfweight Manor.

00:03:19.296 --> 00:03:25.289
Mrs. Medlock, her uncle's housekeeper, met Mary in London.

00:03:25.349 --> 00:03:29.371
Mary disliked Mrs. Medlock immediately.

00:03:29.431 --> 00:03:34.415
But this was nothing new because Mary disliked everyone.

00:03:34.475 --> 00:03:38.018
Mrs. Medlock did not like Mary.

00:03:38.078 --> 00:03:45.202
She thought that the little girl was bad-tempered, rude and plain, and she was right.

00:03:45.262 --> 00:03:53.546
During the long train journey to Yorkshire, Mrs. Medlock told Mary about the house where she was going to live.

00:03:53.606 --> 00:03:59.684
It seemed very large and gloomy, and it was near the edge of a moor.

00:03:59.744 --> 00:04:06.872
There's nothing for you to do there, and your uncle is not interested in you," said Mrs. Medlock.

00:04:06.932 --> 00:04:08.762
He's got a crooked back.

00:04:08.822 --> 00:04:12.363
He was a sour young man until he married.

00:04:12.423 --> 00:04:15.454
Mary listened more carefully now.

00:04:15.514 --> 00:04:18.695
She did not know that her uncle was married.

00:04:18.755 --> 00:04:23.060
His wife was very pretty, and he loved her very much.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.407
When she died, he became even stranger.

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:28.129
Mrs. Medlock said.

00:04:28.188 --> 00:04:29.830
Oh, did she die?

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:31.902
Asked Mary, yes.

00:04:31.962 --> 00:04:34.084
And now he likes nobody.

00:04:34.143 --> 00:04:41.209
He's away most of the time, so you must look after yourself.

00:04:41.269 --> 00:04:48.381
It was dark and raining when they got out of the train.

00:04:48.441 --> 00:04:57.084
They travelled to the house by horse and carriage, but Mary could see nothing outside because of the rain and the darkness of the night.

00:04:57.144 --> 00:04:58.396
What is the more?

00:04:58.456 --> 00:04:59.877
Mary asked.

00:04:59.937 --> 00:05:04.160
It's miles and miles of land, replied Mrs. Medlock.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:10.295
Very little growth on it, and nothing lives on it, except ponies and sheep.

00:05:10.355 --> 00:05:15.540
The carriage stopped at last in a courtyard.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:21.583
A butler opened a heavy wooden door.

00:05:21.643 --> 00:05:25.004
Take her to her room.

00:05:25.064 --> 00:05:27.104
He said to Mrs. Medlock.

00:05:27.164 --> 00:05:29.875
The master doesn't want to see her.

00:05:29.935 --> 00:05:32.325
He's going to London tomorrow.

00:05:32.385 --> 00:05:40.887
Mrs. Medlock took Mary upstairs, along many corridors to a room with a fire burning in it and food on the table.

00:05:40.947 --> 00:05:42.977
Well, here you are.

00:05:43.037 --> 00:05:44.588
Said Mrs. Medlock.

00:05:44.648 --> 00:05:46.640
This is where you'll live.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.874
This room and the next is where you must stay.

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:53.026
You can't go into the other parts of the house.

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:55.176
Don't forget that.

00:05:55.236 --> 00:06:01.640
Mary Lennox felt terribly alone.

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:09.659
Chapter 2 Mary visits the gardens.

00:06:09.719 --> 00:06:17.736
The next morning, Mary woke up when a young housemate came into her room to light the fire.

00:06:17.796 --> 00:06:23.228
Her name was Martha and she talked to Mary while she worked.

00:06:23.287 --> 00:06:27.728
Mary didn't understand servants who were friendly.

00:06:27.788 --> 00:06:32.659
In India, she had spoken to servants only to give them orders.

00:06:32.719 --> 00:06:36.978
She never said, please or thank you.

00:06:37.038 --> 00:06:42.860
Once, she had even slapped her eye as face when she was angry with her.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:49.202
Somehow, she knew that she must not behave in this way with Martha.

00:06:49.262 --> 00:07:00.349
At first, Mary did not listen to Martha, but after a while, she began to like the sound of the friendly Yorkshire voice.

00:07:00.409 --> 00:07:07.155
You should see all my little brothers and sisters in our little cottage on the moor," Martha said.

00:07:07.214 --> 00:07:11.809
There's twelve of us, and my father only earns sixteen shillings a week.

00:07:11.868 --> 00:07:14.561
It is hard for my mother to feed them all.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:17.854
The fresh air on the moor makes them strong and healthy.

00:07:17.914 --> 00:07:19.684
Ah, Dickens, twelve.

00:07:19.744 --> 00:07:21.626
He's always out on the moor.

00:07:21.686 --> 00:07:23.558
He's good with animals.

00:07:23.618 --> 00:07:26.180
He's tamed a wild pony.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:30.089
Go and look at the gardens, Martha said.

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:34.308
There's not much growing now, but they're lovely in summer."

00:07:34.368 --> 00:07:39.322
She paused for a moment, and then said quietly.

00:07:39.382 --> 00:07:42.144
One of the gardens is locked up.

00:07:42.204 --> 00:07:44.496
No one has been in it for ten years.

00:07:44.556 --> 00:07:45.506
Why?

00:07:45.566 --> 00:07:47.558
asked Mary.

00:07:47.618 --> 00:07:51.181
Mr. Craven closed it after his wife died.

00:07:51.241 --> 00:07:53.042
It was her garden.

00:07:53.102 --> 00:07:57.200
He locked the door, dug a hole and buried the key.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:04.920
The enormous grounds of mistlethweight manner were divided by high walls into many gardens.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:09.072
In some there were flowers, trees and fountains.

00:08:09.132 --> 00:08:11.514
Vegetables grew in others.

00:08:11.574 --> 00:08:15.276
Doors opened from garden into garden.

00:08:15.336 --> 00:08:20.820
Because it was winter, the trees were bare and no flowers grew.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:26.593
Mary thought that it all looked very empty and ugly.

00:08:26.653 --> 00:08:31.424
After a while, an old man came through one of the doors.

00:08:31.483 --> 00:08:37.235
He had a surly old face, and did not seem at all pleased to see Mary.

00:08:37.295 --> 00:08:39.126
Can I go through that door?

00:08:39.186 --> 00:08:40.646
Mary asked.

00:08:40.706 --> 00:08:42.197
If you like.

00:08:42.257 --> 00:08:43.237
He replied.

00:08:43.297 --> 00:08:45.738
There's nothing to see.

00:08:45.798 --> 00:08:50.790
Mary hoped that she might find the door to the locked garden.

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:55.690
She tried many doors, but they all opened easily.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:09:02.832
Then she noticed one wall that was covered in ivy, but seemed to have no door in it.

00:09:02.892 --> 00:09:07.562
She could see tall trees behind the ivy covered wall.

00:09:07.622 --> 00:09:12.074
A robin on a high branch started to sing.

00:09:12.134 --> 00:09:20.786
She stopped to listen, and the little bird with the red breast seemed almost to be calling to her.

00:09:20.846 --> 00:09:27.340
His cheerful song brought a small smile to her sad face.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:31.513
The old man continued digging.

00:09:31.573 --> 00:09:35.324
He ignored Mary until at last, she said.

00:09:35.384 --> 00:09:37.966
There's a garden over there without a door.

00:09:38.026 --> 00:09:39.336
What garden?

00:09:39.396 --> 00:09:41.457
He asked, angrily.

00:09:41.517 --> 00:09:43.438
On the other side of the wall?

00:09:43.498 --> 00:09:44.598
She answered.

00:09:44.658 --> 00:09:47.570
I saw a robin in the trees over there.

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:54.323
The old man stopped digging, and to Mary's surprise, he smiled.

00:09:54.383 --> 00:09:57.624
He looked quite different when he smiled.

00:09:57.684 --> 00:10:02.264
He whistled very softly.

00:10:02.324 --> 00:10:07.726
Then a wonderful thing happened.

00:10:07.786 --> 00:10:13.597
There was a sound of wings, and the robin came down next to the man's foot.

00:10:13.657 --> 00:10:15.287
Here he is.

00:10:15.347 --> 00:10:17.812
The old man chuckled.

00:10:17.872 --> 00:10:21.668
He always comes to me when I whistle.

00:10:21.728 --> 00:10:24.680
Isn't he a nice little bird?

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:28.882
The robin hopped about, pecking at the earth.

00:10:28.942 --> 00:10:33.035
The gardener, Ben Weatherstaff, continued digging.

00:10:33.055 --> 00:10:35.916
He's the only friend I've got.

00:10:35.976 --> 00:10:39.138
He said, I've never had any friends.

00:10:39.198 --> 00:10:41.519
Said Mary, sadly.

00:10:41.579 --> 00:10:44.932
Ben stopped digging and looked at Mary.

00:10:44.992 --> 00:10:47.444
You and I are the same then.

00:10:47.504 --> 00:10:53.328
He said to her, We're not good looking and we're as sour as we'll look.

00:10:53.388 --> 00:11:00.772
It was the first time that Mary had ever thought about her angry face and bad temper.

00:11:00.832 --> 00:11:05.244
Now that she did, she felt uncomfortable.

00:11:05.304 --> 00:11:13.048
Just then, the clear sound of the Robin song made her look towards the apple tree where he sat.

00:11:13.108 --> 00:11:17.409
Ben Weatherstaff laughed.

00:11:17.469 --> 00:11:21.150
What did he do that for?

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.241
Asked Mary.

00:11:22.261 --> 00:11:25.262
He's decided to be your friend.

00:11:25.322 --> 00:11:26.633
Replied Ben.

00:11:26.693 --> 00:11:28.784
He's taken a fancy to you.

00:11:28.804 --> 00:11:35.707
To me, said Mary, and she moved softly towards the little tree and looked up.

00:11:35.767 --> 00:11:37.498
Would you make friends with me?

00:11:37.558 --> 00:11:42.498
She said gently to the robin as if she was speaking to a person.

00:11:42.558 --> 00:11:44.058
Why?

00:11:44.118 --> 00:11:45.990
said Ben quietly.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:50.884
You said that like a real child instead of a little old woman.

00:11:50.944 --> 00:11:56.888
You said it almost like Dickon when he talks to his wild things out on the moor.

00:11:56.948 --> 00:11:59.710
The robin flew over the wall.

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:03.768
There must be a door to that garden, Mary said firmly.

00:12:03.828 --> 00:12:10.589
There's no door that you can find, and in any case, it's none of your business.

00:12:10.649 --> 00:12:12.440
Ben said sharply.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:16.914
Don't poke your nose in where it doesn't belong.

00:12:16.974 --> 00:12:23.090
The gardener walked away without saying goodbye.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:35.440
Chapter 3 A Cry in the Night Mary spent most of her days outside in the grounds.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:43.243
The cold wind made her cheeks pink, and each evening she ate all of her food.

00:12:43.302 --> 00:12:48.444
After dinner, she liked to sit near the fire and talk to Martha.

00:12:48.504 --> 00:12:51.294
Why does Mr Craven hate the locked garden?

00:12:51.354 --> 00:12:53.884
Mary asked once.

00:12:53.945 --> 00:12:56.835
It was Mrs. Craven's garden.

00:12:56.895 --> 00:12:58.066
She loved it.

00:12:58.126 --> 00:13:01.418
She and Mr. Craven looked after the flowers together.

00:13:01.478 --> 00:13:03.509
No gardeners were allowed in.

00:13:03.569 --> 00:13:05.090
But what happened?

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.942
Mary asked impatiently.

00:13:08.002 --> 00:13:12.824
Mrs. Craven was sitting on a branch of a tree when it broke and she fell.

00:13:12.884 --> 00:13:15.636
She was injured so badly she died.

00:13:15.696 --> 00:13:18.518
That's why Mr. Craven hates the garden.

00:13:18.578 --> 00:13:22.003
It won't let anyone ever talk about it.

00:13:22.063 --> 00:13:31.570
Mary had never felt sorry for anyone before, but now she realized how unhappy her uncle must be.

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:37.692
The wind moaned around the house, banging at the doors and windows.

00:13:37.752 --> 00:13:41.553
Martha said it was wothering.

00:13:41.613 --> 00:13:48.936
Mary listened, and through the noise, she thought that she heard a child crying.

00:13:48.996 --> 00:13:51.426
Do you hear someone crying?

00:13:51.486 --> 00:13:53.482
She asked Martha.

00:13:53.542 --> 00:13:56.739
Martha suddenly looked confused.

00:13:56.799 --> 00:13:59.620
No, she answered.

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:02.421
It's only the wind or the scullery made.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:05.392
She's cried all day with too thick.

00:14:05.452 --> 00:14:09.392
Then Martha quickly left the room.

00:14:09.452 --> 00:14:12.484
Next day it rained.

00:14:12.544 --> 00:14:17.640
Mary was bored and complained to Martha that she had nothing to do.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:23.888
On a day like this at home, we all try to keep busy indoors," Martha said.

00:14:23.948 --> 00:14:25.638
Except Dickon.

00:14:25.698 --> 00:14:28.920
He goes out on the moor in all types of weather.

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:31.682
He brought home a fox cub that he found.

00:14:31.742 --> 00:14:36.284
He's got a crow tool called suit.

00:14:36.344 --> 00:14:43.848
When Martha left her alone, Mary decided to explore the house.

00:14:43.908 --> 00:14:48.796
She went along corridors and up and down stairs.

00:14:48.856 --> 00:14:56.169
In the silence of the house, she heard again the sound of a child crying.

00:14:56.229 --> 00:15:05.477
She stopped to listen at a door, but then another door opened and out came Mrs Medlock.

00:15:05.537 --> 00:15:07.118
What are you doing here?

00:15:07.178 --> 00:15:11.062
She said, and she took Mary by the arm and pulled her away.

00:15:11.122 --> 00:15:13.434
Get back to your room at once.

00:15:13.494 --> 00:15:17.696
I didn't know which way to go, and then I heard someone crying.

00:15:17.756 --> 00:15:18.867
Said Mary.

00:15:18.927 --> 00:15:22.319
You didn't hear anything, said Mrs. Medlock.

00:15:22.379 --> 00:15:27.282
Go back to your room, or I'll tell the master that you disobeyed him."

00:15:27.342 --> 00:15:30.074
Mary was angry.

00:15:30.134 --> 00:15:33.458
She wanted to know what the cry was.

00:15:33.518 --> 00:15:36.620
Soon the storm passed.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:41.922
Wait until the sun shines and lights up the moor, said Martha.

00:15:41.982 --> 00:15:47.382
I'd love to see your cottage on the moor and meet your mother," said Mary.

00:15:47.442 --> 00:15:50.873
You would like my mother, Martha said.

00:15:50.932 --> 00:15:54.123
She's kind and good-tempered and works hard.

00:15:54.183 --> 00:15:58.895
When it's my day off and I can go home and see her, I'd jump for joy.

00:15:58.955 --> 00:16:00.935
I'd like to see Dickham too.

00:16:00.995 --> 00:16:02.206
Said Mary.

00:16:02.266 --> 00:16:05.316
Yes, you'd like him, Martha said.

00:16:05.377 --> 00:16:07.167
Everyone likes Dickham.

00:16:07.227 --> 00:16:08.908
No one likes me.

00:16:08.968 --> 00:16:11.077
Said Mary, sadly.

00:16:11.137 --> 00:16:14.088
Maybe that's because you don't like yourself?

00:16:14.148 --> 00:16:15.770
Laughed Martha.

00:16:15.829 --> 00:16:17.720
I never thought of that.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.792
Said Mary.

00:16:19.852 --> 00:16:24.126
Mary found Ben Weatherstaff working in the garden.

00:16:24.185 --> 00:16:25.847
Springs come in.

00:16:25.907 --> 00:16:26.908
He said.

00:16:26.968 --> 00:16:30.140
The plants are growing under the soil.

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:34.524
Soon you'll see crocuses and daffodils.

00:16:34.584 --> 00:16:39.782
Mary saw that the robin was on a wall covered with ivy.

00:16:39.842 --> 00:16:43.558
He hopped down to the soil at her feet.

00:16:43.618 --> 00:16:47.329
The robin tried to find a worm in the garden.

00:16:47.389 --> 00:16:52.691
Suddenly, Mary saw an old, rusty key.

00:16:52.751 --> 00:16:55.742
Perhaps it's been buried for ten years.

00:16:55.802 --> 00:16:57.223
She said to herself.

00:16:57.283 --> 00:16:59.464
Perhaps it's the key to the garden.

00:16:59.524 --> 00:17:03.226
She thought, putting it into her pocket.

00:17:03.286 --> 00:17:09.226
After supper, Martha told Mary all about her day at home.

00:17:09.286 --> 00:17:11.994
Mother has sent you a present?

00:17:12.054 --> 00:17:13.266
She said.

00:17:13.325 --> 00:17:18.999
She brought out a skipping rope with striped handles and showed Mary how to skip.

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:21.101
Your mother is very kind.

00:17:21.161 --> 00:17:22.802
Mary said.

00:17:22.862 --> 00:17:30.168
She wondered how Mary's mother could find the money to buy her the rope with all those hungry mouths to feed.

00:17:30.228 --> 00:17:36.869
Mary skipped all the time and the more she skipped the stronger she grew.

00:17:36.929 --> 00:17:43.808
Her cheeks became red, and her plain face started to look almost pretty.

00:17:43.868 --> 00:17:50.832
One day, as Mary watched the Robin in the garden, a wonderful thing happened.

00:17:50.892 --> 00:17:55.004
To Mary, it was almost like magic.

00:17:55.064 --> 00:18:04.842
A small gust of wind blew aside some of the ivy on the wall, and beneath the leaves she saw a door.

00:18:04.902 --> 00:18:08.478
She remembered that she had the key in her pocket.

00:18:08.538 --> 00:18:17.144
She tried it in the lock, and although it was very stiff, she turned it.

00:18:17.204 --> 00:18:25.801
The next moment, she stood inside the secret garden.

00:18:25.861 --> 00:18:33.622
It was the loveliest and most mysterious looking place that Mary had seen.

00:18:33.682 --> 00:18:41.873
It was overgrown and untidy, but she could see plants starting to push their way up through the soil.

00:18:41.933 --> 00:18:46.756
She pulled weeds away to make space for the spring flowers to grow.

00:18:46.816 --> 00:18:49.118
Now they look as if they can breathe.

00:18:49.178 --> 00:18:50.480
She thought.

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:53.642
Then she whispered to herself.

00:18:53.702 --> 00:18:58.736
I am the first person who has spoken in here for ten years.

00:18:58.796 --> 00:19:03.880
Time passed quickly as Mary cleared the weeds and dead grass.

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:08.574
Soon it was time to go back to the house for her supper.

00:19:08.634 --> 00:19:15.618
Mary wanted to tell Martha her secret, but she knew that this was not a good idea.

00:19:15.678 --> 00:19:25.162
She might be forbidden to go into the secret garden again, so instead she said, I would like a little garden to grow things in.

00:19:25.222 --> 00:19:29.725
Why, that's just what you need to keep you busy, said Martha.

00:19:29.785 --> 00:19:34.874
I'll get Dickon to bring some garden tools and some seeds to plant.

00:19:34.934 --> 00:19:40.114
Mary worked with her hands each day in the secret garden.

00:19:40.174 --> 00:19:44.887
She was careful not to let Ben weatherstaff see where she went.

00:19:44.948 --> 00:19:48.620
But Ben noticed a change in her.

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:53.404
One day he said, The fresher is good for you.

00:19:53.464 --> 00:19:58.720
You're less thin and your skin is less yellow.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:02.052
Chapter 4.

00:20:02.113 --> 00:20:09.046
Dickon One day, Mary saw a boy sitting under a tree.

00:20:09.106 --> 00:20:12.437
He seemed about 12 years old.

00:20:12.497 --> 00:20:14.867
He played on a pipe.

00:20:14.928 --> 00:20:18.618
Two rabbits and a squirrel were near him.

00:20:18.678 --> 00:20:24.340
They seemed to listen to the tune he played.

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:31.720
The boy got up carefully because he didn't want to frighten the animals.

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:36.429
He had blue eyes and a round pink face.

00:20:36.489 --> 00:20:38.950
I'm Deacon, he said to Mary.

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:42.612
I brought the garden tools and some flower seeds.

00:20:42.672 --> 00:20:49.594
Deacon had a kind and gentle smile, and Mary felt that she knew him quite well.

00:20:49.654 --> 00:20:55.980
She felt that if the wild animals could trust him, then she could trust him too.

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:58.323
Do you know about the secret garden?"

00:20:58.383 --> 00:20:59.424
asked Mary.

00:20:59.484 --> 00:21:00.994
I've heard about it.

00:21:01.054 --> 00:21:02.075
Dicken answered.

00:21:02.135 --> 00:21:04.096
But I don't know where it is.

00:21:04.156 --> 00:21:05.287
Come with me.

00:21:05.347 --> 00:21:07.038
Mary said.

00:21:07.098 --> 00:21:10.460
Mary was careful that no one saw them.

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:14.262
And then she took Dicken through the door in the wall.

00:21:14.322 --> 00:21:17.064
Dicken was very surprised.

00:21:17.124 --> 00:21:19.775
This is a strange, pretty place.

00:21:19.835 --> 00:21:20.826
He said.

00:21:20.886 --> 00:21:23.869
It's like being in a dream.

00:21:23.929 --> 00:21:29.646
Dicken looked around at all the plants and trees which Mary thought were dead.

00:21:29.706 --> 00:21:32.448
All of these will grow, he said.

00:21:32.508 --> 00:21:37.532
There'll be flowers and roses everywhere in a few weeks.

00:21:37.592 --> 00:21:43.637
Dicken and Mary worked together to clear away the weeds and dead wood.

00:21:43.698 --> 00:21:48.604
Mary felt that she had never known anyone like Dicken.

00:21:48.664 --> 00:21:55.019
She tried to speak in a warm, friendly voice, like Dickens and Martha's.

00:21:55.079 --> 00:21:56.370
Do you like me?

00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:57.400
She asked.

00:21:57.461 --> 00:21:58.581
Yes, I do.

00:21:58.641 --> 00:21:59.832
He laughed.

00:21:59.892 --> 00:22:02.654
The Rubble likes you too.

00:22:02.714 --> 00:22:09.007
That evening, after dinner, Mrs. Medlock took Mary to see Mr. Craven.

00:22:09.067 --> 00:22:15.070
He's going abroad tomorrow, and he wants to see you first, she said.

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:18.476
Mary felt a little afraid.

00:22:18.536 --> 00:22:24.960
She felt sure that she would not like Mr. Craven and that he would not like her.

00:22:25.020 --> 00:22:32.352
But she found that Mr. Craven wasn't really frightening and that his back wasn't really crooked.

00:22:32.412 --> 00:22:38.284
His face was handsome, but he looked sad and worried.

00:22:38.344 --> 00:22:42.885
He asked Mary if there was anything that she would like.

00:22:42.945 --> 00:22:48.318
Mary asked for a piece of garden in which to grow her own flowers.

00:22:48.378 --> 00:22:49.801
Of course.

00:22:49.861 --> 00:22:51.052
Set her uncle.

00:22:51.112 --> 00:22:54.314
You may take any bit that is not used.

00:22:54.374 --> 00:22:56.646
Mary was delighted.

00:22:56.706 --> 00:23:00.710
Now she could have the secret garden for herself.

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:07.186
That same night, Mary was awakened by the wind roaring around the house.

00:23:07.246 --> 00:23:09.186
She couldn't sleep.

00:23:09.246 --> 00:23:15.424
And as she lay in bed, she heard the crying noise again.

00:23:15.484 --> 00:23:20.110
That's not the wind, she thought.

00:23:20.170 --> 00:23:23.443
I'm going to find out where that noise is coming from.

00:23:23.504 --> 00:23:28.858
Mary took a candle to light her way along the dark corridors.

00:23:28.918 --> 00:23:34.022
Suddenly she noticed a light from under one of the doors.

00:23:34.082 --> 00:23:40.800
The crying sound came from behind the door and Mary knew that it was a child.

00:23:40.860 --> 00:23:50.849
She gently opened the door and saw that a young boy lay on the bed crying.

00:23:50.909 --> 00:23:56.282
When the boy saw Mary, he stopped crying at once.

00:23:56.342 --> 00:23:57.893
Are you a ghost?

00:23:57.953 --> 00:23:59.044
He asked.

00:23:59.104 --> 00:24:01.305
He looked very frightened.

00:24:01.365 --> 00:24:03.376
No, I'm Mary Lennox.

00:24:03.436 --> 00:24:04.366
She answered.

00:24:04.426 --> 00:24:07.224
Who are you?

00:24:07.284 --> 00:24:15.874
Chapter 5 Colin I'm Colin, Mr Cravenson.

00:24:15.934 --> 00:24:17.155
Said the boy.

00:24:17.215 --> 00:24:19.056
Then I must be your cousin.

00:24:19.116 --> 00:24:20.076
Mary said.

00:24:20.136 --> 00:24:22.087
Don't you know that I came to live here?

00:24:22.147 --> 00:24:22.718
No.

00:24:22.778 --> 00:24:23.628
He answered.

00:24:23.688 --> 00:24:25.069
No one told me.

00:24:25.129 --> 00:24:26.089
Why?

00:24:26.149 --> 00:24:27.200
Asked Mary.

00:24:27.260 --> 00:24:30.192
Because I am afraid that people will see me.

00:24:30.252 --> 00:24:33.505
I won't let people see me and talk about me.

00:24:33.565 --> 00:24:34.488
Why?

00:24:34.548 --> 00:24:35.838
asked Mary.

00:24:35.898 --> 00:24:39.860
She felt more puzzled with each moment that passed.

00:24:39.920 --> 00:24:44.154
Because I'm always ill and I must stay in bed.

00:24:44.214 --> 00:24:47.385
The servants are not allowed to speak about me.

00:24:47.446 --> 00:24:50.408
My father won't let anyone mention me.

00:24:50.468 --> 00:24:53.599
He's afraid I'll grow up to have a crooked back.

00:24:53.660 --> 00:24:57.964
My father hates me because my mother died when I was born.

00:24:58.024 --> 00:24:59.876
Have you always been here?

00:24:59.936 --> 00:25:00.937
asked Mary.

00:25:00.997 --> 00:25:02.258
Near you always?

00:25:02.318 --> 00:25:03.359
said Colin.

00:25:03.419 --> 00:25:07.252
If I go out, people stare at me and I hate it.

00:25:07.312 --> 00:25:09.444
If you don't like people to see you.

00:25:09.504 --> 00:25:10.415
Mary said.

00:25:10.475 --> 00:25:11.655
Shall I go away?

00:25:11.716 --> 00:25:12.436
Oh no.

00:25:12.496 --> 00:25:14.388
Colin replied quickly.

00:25:14.448 --> 00:25:17.020
You must stay and talk to me.

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:23.425
Mary put her candle down on a table near the bed and sat on a chair.

00:25:23.485 --> 00:25:26.448
They talked for a long time.

00:25:26.508 --> 00:25:32.569
Colin wanted to know all about Mary and about her life at Misslethwaite.

00:25:32.630 --> 00:25:39.722
He told her how unhappy and lonely he was, even though he was given anything that he wanted.

00:25:39.782 --> 00:25:42.672
Everyone must do as I say.

00:25:42.732 --> 00:25:45.813
Colin said, I will be ill if they don't.

00:25:45.873 --> 00:25:47.814
Do you think you will get well?

00:25:47.874 --> 00:25:49.004
Mary asked.

00:25:49.064 --> 00:25:50.685
I don't suppose I will.

00:25:50.745 --> 00:25:51.855
Colin answered.

00:25:51.915 --> 00:25:55.180
No one believes I will live until I grow up.

00:25:55.240 --> 00:25:57.714
Let's talk about something else.

00:25:57.774 --> 00:25:59.324
How old are you?

00:25:59.384 --> 00:26:01.165
I'm ten, like you.

00:26:01.225 --> 00:26:02.136
Mary said.

00:26:02.196 --> 00:26:03.866
How do you know I'm ten?

00:26:03.926 --> 00:26:04.827
He asked.

00:26:04.887 --> 00:26:09.429
Because when you were born, your father locked the garden door and buried the key.

00:26:09.489 --> 00:26:11.380
It's been locked for ten years.

00:26:11.440 --> 00:26:12.480
Mary answered.

00:26:12.540 --> 00:26:13.551
What garden?

00:26:13.611 --> 00:26:14.751
Colin asked.

00:26:14.811 --> 00:26:17.172
It was the garden Mr Craven hates.

00:26:17.232 --> 00:26:19.273
Said Mary nervously.

00:26:19.333 --> 00:26:20.874
He locked the door.

00:26:20.934 --> 00:26:23.146
No one knew where he buried the key.

00:26:23.206 --> 00:26:25.019
What's the garden like?

00:26:25.079 --> 00:26:26.670
Colin persisted.

00:26:26.730 --> 00:26:28.831
It's been locked for ten years.

00:26:28.891 --> 00:26:31.132
Mary said, carefully.

00:26:31.192 --> 00:26:34.685
She did not want him to know that she had found it.

00:26:34.745 --> 00:26:37.136
But it was too late to be careful.

00:26:37.196 --> 00:26:41.359
Colin was very excited at the idea of a hidden garden.

00:26:41.419 --> 00:26:43.590
I will make them open the door.

00:26:43.650 --> 00:26:44.581
He said.

00:26:44.641 --> 00:26:45.572
Oh no!

00:26:45.632 --> 00:26:46.702
Cried Mary.

00:26:46.762 --> 00:26:48.674
Let's keep it a secret.

00:26:48.734 --> 00:26:52.204
If they open the door, it will never be a secret again.

00:26:52.264 --> 00:26:57.534
If we find the door one day, we can go inside and no one will know about it except us.

00:26:57.595 --> 00:26:58.765
I would like that."

00:26:58.825 --> 00:26:59.675
said Colin.

00:26:59.735 --> 00:27:02.036
I've never had a secret before.

00:27:02.096 --> 00:27:10.058
He was tired from talking, and as he fell asleep, Mary went quietly away.

00:27:10.118 --> 00:27:21.310
Chapter 6 Wet Weather Next morning, Mary told Martha that she had found Colin.

00:27:21.370 --> 00:27:23.710
Martha was very upset.

00:27:23.770 --> 00:27:28.343
She thought that she could lose her job for allowing Mary to find the young boy.

00:27:28.403 --> 00:27:30.545
Don't worry, said Mary.

00:27:30.605 --> 00:27:32.616
Colin was pleased to see me.

00:27:32.676 --> 00:27:35.068
He wants to see me every day.

00:27:35.128 --> 00:27:38.652
You must have bewitched him, said Martha.

00:27:38.712 --> 00:27:40.563
What's the matter with him?

00:27:40.623 --> 00:27:42.564
Mary asked.

00:27:42.625 --> 00:27:47.008
Martha told Mary that Colin had never been allowed to walk.

00:27:47.068 --> 00:27:50.406
His father thought that his back was weak.

00:27:50.466 --> 00:28:01.992
Even though a famous doctor had examined him and said that he would get strong if less fuss was made of him, Colin was still spoiled and allowed to do everything that he wanted.

00:28:02.052 --> 00:28:06.036
Colin thinks he will die, said Mary.

00:28:06.096 --> 00:28:12.872
Mother says that he has no reason to live if he's closed up in his room all the time, said Martha.

00:28:12.933 --> 00:28:16.105
It's good for me to be outside, said Mary.

00:28:16.165 --> 00:28:18.415
Do you think that it would help Colin?

00:28:18.475 --> 00:28:21.496
Oh, I don't know," Martha said.

00:28:21.556 --> 00:28:25.368
He had a bad temper tantrum when he was taken into the garden.

00:28:25.428 --> 00:28:28.992
He was upset because he thought one of the gardeners was looking at him.

00:28:29.052 --> 00:28:31.354
He cried until he felt ill.

00:28:31.414 --> 00:28:35.516
If he ever gets angry with me, I won't go to see him again.

00:28:35.577 --> 00:28:37.258
Said Mary.

00:28:37.318 --> 00:28:42.423
When Mary next went to see Colin, she told him about Dickon.

00:28:42.484 --> 00:28:45.256
He's not like anyone else, she said.

00:28:45.316 --> 00:28:47.376
All the animals on the moor love him.

00:28:47.436 --> 00:28:49.767
When he places pipe, they come to listen.

00:28:49.827 --> 00:28:52.258
The moor must be a wonderful place.

00:28:52.318 --> 00:28:53.158
Said Colin.

00:28:53.218 --> 00:28:54.648
But I can't go there.

00:28:54.708 --> 00:28:56.339
I'm going to die.

00:28:56.399 --> 00:28:58.019
How do you know that?

00:28:58.080 --> 00:28:59.480
Mary asked.

00:28:59.540 --> 00:29:02.801
She felt a little cross with Colin.

00:29:02.861 --> 00:29:06.495
He seemed to be pleased with the thought that he could die.

00:29:06.555 --> 00:29:09.189
Because everyone says I will die."

00:29:09.249 --> 00:29:10.259
Colin replied.

00:29:10.319 --> 00:29:13.420
I think that my father will be pleased when I'm dead.

00:29:13.480 --> 00:29:14.710
I don't believe that.

00:29:14.770 --> 00:29:15.690
Mary said.

00:29:15.750 --> 00:29:17.621
The famous doctor was right.

00:29:17.681 --> 00:29:21.562
They should make much less fuss of you and allow you to go out.

00:29:21.622 --> 00:29:24.893
If you could see Dickon, you'd want to get well.

00:29:24.953 --> 00:29:33.708
Then Mary told Colin about Dickon's family, who had no money, but were all healthy and cheerful.

00:29:33.768 --> 00:29:39.344
It rained for a week, so Mary could not visit the garden.

00:29:39.404 --> 00:29:44.500
Because the weather was so bad, she spent most of her time with Colin.

00:29:44.560 --> 00:29:50.917
They read books and talked together, and for the first time, Mary heard Colin laugh.

00:29:50.977 --> 00:29:56.866
Colin often spoke about the secret garden and wondered what was in it.

00:29:56.926 --> 00:30:01.214
Mary felt that she could not tell him her secret yet.

00:30:01.274 --> 00:30:05.930
So she still did not tell him that she knew where the mysterious garden was.

00:30:05.990 --> 00:30:09.716
I'll wait until the rain stops before I decide what to do.

00:30:09.776 --> 00:30:11.998
Thought Mary.

00:30:12.058 --> 00:30:20.642
On the day that the rain finished, Mary woke up early to find that the sunlight was streaming through her windows.

00:30:20.702 --> 00:30:26.046
She went quickly to the secret garden, and she found that Dickon was already there.

00:30:26.106 --> 00:30:29.938
I couldn't stay in bed in the morning like this, he said.

00:30:29.998 --> 00:30:31.809
Look at the garden.

00:30:31.869 --> 00:30:37.802
The rain and sunshine had made the new plant start to come through the earth.

00:30:37.862 --> 00:30:42.050
There were some purple, orange and gold crocuses.

00:30:42.110 --> 00:30:46.265
Mary was very pleased to see them, and she kissed them.

00:30:46.325 --> 00:30:48.586
The Robin was building a nest.

00:30:48.646 --> 00:30:50.656
We mustn't watch too closely.

00:30:50.716 --> 00:30:51.557
Dickens said.

00:30:51.617 --> 00:30:55.368
He'll stay here with us if we don't fight in him.

00:30:55.428 --> 00:30:59.749
A whole week had gone by since Mary had seen Dickens.

00:30:59.809 --> 00:31:02.520
She told him that she had found Colin.

00:31:02.580 --> 00:31:06.211
If he comes out here in the garden, he'll forget that he's ill.

00:31:06.271 --> 00:31:07.122
Dickens said.

00:31:07.182 --> 00:31:12.348
He'll be another child, looking at the flowers and animals like us.

00:31:12.408 --> 00:31:21.500
When Mary went back to the house at the end of the day, Martha told her that Colin was angry because she had not been to see him.

00:31:21.560 --> 00:31:26.374
I won't allow that boy to come here if you stay with him instead of me.

00:31:26.434 --> 00:31:27.526
Colin said.

00:31:27.586 --> 00:31:31.118
If you send Dick away, I'll never come into this room again.

00:31:31.178 --> 00:31:32.370
Mary replied.

00:31:32.430 --> 00:31:33.581
You're selfish.

00:31:33.641 --> 00:31:35.001
Colin raged.

00:31:35.062 --> 00:31:36.473
What about you?

00:31:36.533 --> 00:31:38.612
Mary replied furiously.

00:31:38.672 --> 00:31:41.070
You're the most selfish boy I know.

00:31:41.130 --> 00:31:43.152
Well, I'm going to die."

00:31:43.212 --> 00:31:44.173
Colin said.

00:31:44.233 --> 00:31:46.425
No, you're not, Mary replied.

00:31:46.485 --> 00:31:52.230
You just say that to make people feel sorry for you, but they don't feel sorry, you're too nasty.

00:31:52.290 --> 00:31:55.844
Mary marched to the door and then said angrily.

00:31:55.904 --> 00:32:01.078
I was going to tell you all about Dickon and his fox and crow, but I won't now.

00:32:01.138 --> 00:32:04.584
She slammed the door behind her.

00:32:04.644 --> 00:32:11.221
Later, when Mary remembered how lonely Colin was, she felt sorry for him.

00:32:11.281 --> 00:32:13.042
I'll go and see him tomorrow.

00:32:13.102 --> 00:32:13.883
She thought.

00:32:13.943 --> 00:32:15.664
I'll go and sit with him.

00:32:15.724 --> 00:32:22.120
Later that night, Mary was awakened by the sound of screaming and crying.

00:32:22.180 --> 00:32:25.424
It's Colin having one of his tempers.

00:32:25.484 --> 00:32:26.566
She thought.

00:32:26.625 --> 00:32:32.700
She put her hands over her ears, but she could not block out the terrible noise.

00:32:32.760 --> 00:32:35.241
Someone should stop him, she cried.

00:32:35.302 --> 00:32:38.154
He deserves to be punished for being so selfish.

00:32:38.214 --> 00:32:40.405
He's woken everyone in the house.

00:32:40.465 --> 00:32:44.188
She ran into Colin's room and shouted at him.

00:32:44.248 --> 00:32:44.998
Stop!

00:32:45.058 --> 00:32:46.129
I hate you!

00:32:46.189 --> 00:32:47.370
Everyone hates you.

00:32:47.430 --> 00:32:51.589
You'll scream until you die, and I hope that you do.

00:32:51.649 --> 00:32:54.927
Chapter seven.

00:32:54.987 --> 00:32:58.620
I will live forever and ever.

00:32:58.680 --> 00:33:01.942
Colin looked terrible.

00:33:02.002 --> 00:33:07.925
His face was swollen from crying, but Mary was too angry to care.

00:33:07.985 --> 00:33:10.897
If you scream again, then I will scream louder.

00:33:10.957 --> 00:33:12.098
She told him.

00:33:12.158 --> 00:33:14.069
I can't stop.

00:33:14.129 --> 00:33:15.400
Colin sobbed.

00:33:15.460 --> 00:33:18.212
There's something wrong with my back.

00:33:18.272 --> 00:33:21.859
I will have a crooked back and then I will die.

00:33:21.919 --> 00:33:24.536
Turn over and let me look at your back."

00:33:24.596 --> 00:33:26.138
Mary said.

00:33:26.198 --> 00:33:30.594
She looked at the poor, thin back for a long time.

00:33:30.654 --> 00:33:32.255
There's nothing wrong with it.

00:33:32.315 --> 00:33:34.067
Your back is as straight as mine.

00:33:34.127 --> 00:33:35.589
She told him.

00:33:35.649 --> 00:33:44.430
Colin stopped crying, and Mary sat by his bed, talking to him quietly until he fell asleep.

00:33:44.490 --> 00:33:51.444
The next morning, Mary met Dickon in the garden, and she told him about Colin crying in the night.

00:33:51.504 --> 00:33:54.115
We must get him out here, poor boy.

00:33:54.175 --> 00:33:55.766
Said Dickon kindly.

00:33:55.826 --> 00:33:57.257
Yes, we must.

00:33:57.317 --> 00:34:01.509
Said Mary, using the same kind Yorkshire voice.

00:34:01.569 --> 00:34:03.090
Dickon laughed.

00:34:03.150 --> 00:34:11.724
Talking your Yorkshire voice to Colin, he said, it'll make him laugh, and Mother says laughing is good for people when they're ill.

00:34:11.785 --> 00:34:14.938
Mary went to see Colin later that day.

00:34:14.998 --> 00:34:20.731
She told him about Dickon and his squirrels who were called Nut and Shell.

00:34:20.792 --> 00:34:26.176
Then Colin said, I'm sorry I said that I would send Dickon away.

00:34:26.236 --> 00:34:28.508
He seems a wonderful boy.

00:34:28.569 --> 00:34:30.190
I'm glad you said that.

00:34:30.250 --> 00:34:31.040
Said Mary.

00:34:31.100 --> 00:34:34.646
Because he's coming to see you and he's bringing his animals.

00:34:34.706 --> 00:34:37.769
Colin suddenly looked cheerful.

00:34:37.829 --> 00:34:43.723
He looked so happy that Mary thought that she would tell him her great secret.

00:34:43.783 --> 00:34:45.764
That's not all, she said.

00:34:45.824 --> 00:34:47.666
There's something even better.

00:34:47.726 --> 00:34:49.956
I found the door to the garden.

00:34:50.017 --> 00:34:52.519
Colin was very pleased.

00:34:52.578 --> 00:34:55.680
Then we can go in and find out what's inside.

00:34:55.740 --> 00:34:57.222
He cried.

00:34:57.282 --> 00:35:02.207
Mary waited for a moment, and then she told him the truth.

00:35:02.267 --> 00:35:03.601
I've been inside.

00:35:03.661 --> 00:35:06.173
That's why I could tell you so much about it.

00:35:06.233 --> 00:35:10.036
I couldn't tell you my secret until I was sure that I could trust you.

00:35:10.096 --> 00:35:13.128
At breakfast, Colin told his nurse.

00:35:13.188 --> 00:35:16.330
A boy and his animals are coming to see me.

00:35:16.390 --> 00:35:19.332
Bring them straight up when they arrive.

00:35:19.392 --> 00:35:24.356
Soon afterwards, Mary heard a bleeding.

00:35:24.417 --> 00:35:27.088
That's Dickens Lam.

00:35:27.148 --> 00:35:28.109
She said.

00:35:28.169 --> 00:35:29.601
They're coming.

00:35:29.662 --> 00:35:31.784
Dickon came in.

00:35:31.844 --> 00:35:33.595
He was smiling.

00:35:33.655 --> 00:35:38.027
He carried a lamb and his little fox followed behind him.

00:35:38.087 --> 00:35:42.110
The squirrel sat on one shoulder and the crow on the other.

00:35:42.170 --> 00:35:44.981
The other squirrel was in his pocket.

00:35:45.041 --> 00:35:48.542
Colin stared in surprise.

00:35:48.602 --> 00:35:53.476
Dickon gave the lamb to Colin and handed him a bottle to feed it.

00:35:53.536 --> 00:35:56.830
The little boy was busy and happy.

00:35:56.890 --> 00:36:01.136
After a while, Colin cried, I must see it all.

00:36:01.196 --> 00:36:03.186
I must see the secret garden.

00:36:03.246 --> 00:36:04.917
Yes, of course you must.

00:36:04.977 --> 00:36:06.068
Said Mary.

00:36:06.128 --> 00:36:09.010
And she must lose no time about it.

00:36:09.070 --> 00:36:15.042
They put Colin in his wheelchair and Dickon pushed it along the garden paths.

00:36:15.102 --> 00:36:21.355
Mary told Colin all about the places they passed on their way to the door that led to the secret garden.

00:36:21.415 --> 00:36:23.396
Here's where I met Ben with the stuff.

00:36:23.456 --> 00:36:26.310
She said, and this is where I saw the Robin.

00:36:26.370 --> 00:36:32.038
Then she said quietly to him, this is a secret garden.

00:36:32.098 --> 00:36:41.426
Mary looked around to make sure that no one was watching and then Dickon pushed the chair quickly inside.

00:36:41.486 --> 00:36:45.550
Colin looked at the trees and flowers.

00:36:45.610 --> 00:36:53.279
He listened to the sweet sound of the bird singing and he felt the warm sun on his face.

00:36:53.339 --> 00:37:00.845
His pale skin started to become pink as he breathed in the good fresh air.

00:37:00.905 --> 00:37:07.138
Then he cried out, I will be well, I will live forever and ever.

00:37:07.197 --> 00:37:10.960
That day, the world changed for Colin.

00:37:11.020 --> 00:37:13.190
It's been a wonderful day.

00:37:13.250 --> 00:37:14.121
Said Dickon.

00:37:14.181 --> 00:37:15.401
It certainly has.

00:37:15.461 --> 00:37:16.642
Replied Mary.

00:37:16.702 --> 00:37:17.712
Do you think?

00:37:17.772 --> 00:37:21.380
Said Colin, that it was made like this just for me.

00:37:21.440 --> 00:37:24.156
You sound almost as Yorkshire as Dickon now.

00:37:24.216 --> 00:37:25.406
Laughed Mary.

00:37:25.466 --> 00:37:29.327
I don't want the state to finish, but I will come back every day.

00:37:29.387 --> 00:37:32.338
Colin said.

00:37:32.398 --> 00:37:35.898
Chapter 8.

00:37:35.958 --> 00:37:37.828
Magic.

00:37:37.888 --> 00:37:39.819
Of course she will.

00:37:39.879 --> 00:37:40.659
Said Dickon.

00:37:40.679 --> 00:37:43.420
She will have you working and walking.

00:37:43.480 --> 00:37:49.818
But suddenly, Ben Weatherstaff's angry face looked down at them from the top of the wall.

00:37:49.879 --> 00:37:51.977
What are you doing in there?

00:37:52.037 --> 00:37:54.668
He shouted angrily at Mary.

00:37:54.728 --> 00:38:00.262
Then he saw Colin and his mouth opened in astonishment.

00:38:00.322 --> 00:38:02.203
Do you know who I am?

00:38:02.263 --> 00:38:03.408
Colin asked.

00:38:03.468 --> 00:38:06.314
Yes, of course I do.

00:38:06.374 --> 00:38:07.545
Ben answered.

00:38:07.605 --> 00:38:10.426
You are the poor boy who's always ill.

00:38:10.486 --> 00:38:12.717
Colin sat up angrily.

00:38:12.777 --> 00:38:14.498
There's nothing wrong with me.

00:38:14.558 --> 00:38:15.628
I'll show you.

00:38:15.688 --> 00:38:16.738
He cried.

00:38:16.799 --> 00:38:22.851
He pulled himself up out of his chair and with Dickens' help he stood up straight and tall.

00:38:22.911 --> 00:38:23.871
Look at me.

00:38:23.932 --> 00:38:25.222
He shouted at Ben.

00:38:25.282 --> 00:38:26.713
Just look at me.

00:38:26.773 --> 00:38:28.974
You dear boy.

00:38:29.034 --> 00:38:32.702
Said Ben, and he cried with happiness.

00:38:32.762 --> 00:38:35.529
Colin stayed standing.

00:38:35.590 --> 00:38:39.612
Suddenly he felt all his fears leave him.

00:38:39.672 --> 00:38:41.474
I'm not afraid anymore.

00:38:41.534 --> 00:38:42.404
He cried.

00:38:42.464 --> 00:38:44.716
It's the magic of the secret garden.

00:38:44.776 --> 00:38:50.080
The magic that made all the plants grow strong has made me grow strong too.

00:38:50.140 --> 00:38:54.692
That evening, when Colin sat with Mary, he was quiet.

00:38:54.752 --> 00:38:58.204
I'm not going to be a poor, sad boy anymore.

00:38:58.264 --> 00:39:03.473
If I believe that I will be stronger and well, then the magic will make it happen.

00:39:03.533 --> 00:39:10.141
The next day, when the children went into the garden, Colin told Dickin and Mary to watch him.

00:39:10.201 --> 00:39:14.293
I'm going to show you that the magic made me well, he said.

00:39:14.353 --> 00:39:19.936
Carefully, taking a few steps at a time, Colin walked around the garden.

00:39:19.996 --> 00:39:22.627
His face glowed with joy.

00:39:22.687 --> 00:39:25.238
Please keep this a secret, he said.

00:39:25.299 --> 00:39:35.754
When I can walk and run really well, I will walk into my father's study and say, Here I am as well and strong as any boy in Yorkshire.

00:39:35.814 --> 00:39:39.506
It was not easy to keep Colin's secret.

00:39:39.566 --> 00:39:45.843
The magic garden made Colin's eyes shine and his pale face become pink.

00:39:45.903 --> 00:39:54.220
Each day Colin and Mary did exercises to make them strong and soon they were happier and healthier.

00:39:54.280 --> 00:39:58.662
Mary looked pretty and Colin didn't look ill anymore.

00:39:58.723 --> 00:40:02.924
Everyone who knew them wondered about the change.

00:40:02.984 --> 00:40:10.728
At the time that the secret garden made its magic for Colin, Mr. Craven travelled in distant countries.

00:40:10.788 --> 00:40:17.063
For ten years he had tried to run away from his sorrow and nothing could comfort him.

00:40:17.124 --> 00:40:23.810
Then, one day while he walked in Austria, he sat down by a stream.

00:40:23.870 --> 00:40:28.382
He felt his mind and his body start to relax.

00:40:28.442 --> 00:40:33.756
The gentle sound of the running water filled him with peace.

00:40:33.816 --> 00:40:40.108
And suddenly, he was both healthy and happy.

00:40:40.168 --> 00:40:47.345
That same night, he dreamt about his wife's garden at Misulfweight Manor.

00:40:47.405 --> 00:40:51.278
The dream made him decide to return home at once.

00:40:51.339 --> 00:40:55.469
As soon as he arrived home, he went to the garden.

00:40:55.529 --> 00:41:04.451
As he walked slowly towards the door of the secret garden, all his sadness came rushing back to him.

00:41:04.511 --> 00:41:12.382
He wondered how he could find the key to the garden, and then he heard laughter from the other side of the wall.

00:41:12.442 --> 00:41:17.890
Then the door opened, and a boy ran out.

00:41:17.950 --> 00:41:24.550
He was a tall, handsome boy, and Mr. Craven gazed at him without speaking.

00:41:24.610 --> 00:41:29.632
Colin stood still and looked at his father in surprise.

00:41:29.692 --> 00:41:34.225
Then he said, Father, I'm Colin, your son.

00:41:34.285 --> 00:41:37.007
You can't believe it, but it's true.

00:41:37.067 --> 00:41:46.276
Colin took his father into the garden and told him how the magic had made the flowers and trees grow and had made him grow strong and healthy.

00:41:46.337 --> 00:41:50.724
Mr. Craven thought that it was a wonderful story.

00:41:50.784 --> 00:41:59.080
He sat down next to Mary, Dickon and the animals, and talked and laughed for the first time in many years.

00:41:59.140 --> 00:42:03.343
He was so proud of his happy, healthy son.

00:42:03.403 --> 00:42:05.675
Now there will be no more secrets.

00:42:05.735 --> 00:42:09.037
Said Colin, I will never need my wheelchair again.

00:42:09.057 --> 00:42:11.940
I will walk with you, Father.

00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:16.195
They all stood up and walked back to the house.

00:42:16.255 --> 00:42:25.564
Mrs. Medlock and Martha watched in amazement as Mr. Craven walked across the lawn, happier than they had ever seen him.

00:42:25.625 --> 00:42:37.763
Next to him, with his head held up high and his eyes full of laughter, walked Colin, as strongly and steadily has any boy in Yorkshire.

